Well, I'm not exactly sure what you are trying to do . . but there is an
easy way to get the fancy walls, etc.  Remember that the xterm tries
to emulate a vt100 (or so).  So if we fix the standard termcap and have
the correct defines for the walls . . you get something that looks pretty
good.

Enclosed below is what I use.  Edit to taste.  It works fine for me.

Note:  This is all from before the -dec option existed, so that it
might not all be necessary.  Also, the environment options are for csh,
so there are extra '\'s in it.

------- environment (the setenv should be all one line)
#
#  Nethack options WITH fancy graphics for xterm.
#
setenv NETHACKOPTIONS "confirm,male,fixinv,nopickup,safe_pet,sortpack,tombstone,
verbose,news,fruit:pineapple,dogname:Dhairrhuwyth,catname:Ghisteslwchlohm,graphi
cs: \o370\o361\o354\o353\o355\o352\o356\o366\o367\o365\o364|-\\/.-|+.#<>\^\o341}
{#\\\o362<>##"

